\ The hand-threaded baseline for Phase 4 slice 6d's dogfood. Its combinator
\ twin `examples/combinator_in_times.sth` expresses the same nested walk over
\ `each` from `lib/combinators.sth`; the golden pins both to the same output.
\ The inner element loop spells out `each`'s own body by hand (a manual
\ `times` loop with the same `&arr i &> @` read), nested directly inside the
\ outer round `times`, the same shape `each`'s internal loop takes once
\ spliced.

import: c | times | "../lib/combinators.sth" ;

: mk ( i64 -- [i64 3] )
  | base | 0 3 fill | s |
  &!s 0 >usize &!> base !
  &!s 1 >usize &!> base 1 + !
  &!s 2 >usize &!> base 2 + !
  s ;

: main ( -- )
  3 [ | i | i mk | arr |
      3 [ | j | &arr j >usize &> @ . ] times
      arr drop
    ] times ;
